-- kondey
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Kondey Island?","answer":"Due to the island''s remote location in the southern atolls, direct public ferry services from Male are limited. Most guesthouses can arrange the complete transfer from Male, including the domestic flight and speedboat connection. When planning your journey, remember that weather conditions can occasionally affect flight schedules in this region, so it''s advisable to allow buffer days in your travel plans. The journey to Kondey is part of the adventure, offering beautiful aerial views of the Maldivian atolls during the flight and a chance to experience the stunning blue waters during the speedboat transfer."},{"question":"What makes Kondey''s fishing culture unique compared to other Maldivian islands?","answer":"Kondey''s fishing culture stands out for its preservation of traditional methods and the central role fishing plays in community life. While fishing is important throughout the Maldives, Kondey has maintained many traditional practices that have been modernized elsewhere. The island''s fishermen still use traditional pole-and-line techniques for tuna fishing, a sustainable method that targets specific species without significant bycatch. Many fishing dhonis (boats) are still built using traditional methods, with local craftsmen maintaining boat-building skills passed down through generations. The community maintains traditional fish processing methods, including smoking and drying techniques that preserve fish without modern refrigeration. Fishing knowledge is still transferred through apprenticeship, with younger community members learning directly from experienced fishermen rather than through formal education. These elements create a living maritime heritage that offers visitors insights into traditional Maldivian fishing culture that is increasingly rare to find in its authentic form."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Kondey Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Kondey Island is during the northeast monsoon season (December to April), which brings dry, sunny weather with lower humidity and calmer seas. This period is ideal for water activities, with excellent visibility for snorkeling and diving. For those interested in experiencing traditional fishing culture, this season also offers more stable conditions for joining fishing excursions. The southwest monsoon (May to November) brings occasional rain showers but also lower prices and fewer tourists. Water temperature remains warm (27-30C/80-86F) throughout the year. Due to Kondey''s southern location, it may experience slightly different weather patterns than northern atolls, with the possibility of brief rain showers even during the dry season. The shoulder months of November and April often offer a good balance of favorable weather and lower visitor numbers."},{"question":"What type of accommodation can I expect on Kondey?","answer":"Accommodation on Kondey is limited and simple, reflecting the island''s authentic character and minimal tourism development. The island offers a small number of family-run guesthouses that provide clean, comfortable rooms with basic amenities including air conditioning, private bathrooms with hot water, and Wi-Fi (though connectivity may be inconsistent). Most accommodations offer full-board packages that include three home-cooked Maldivian meals daily, featuring fresh seafood caught by local fishermen. Some families also offer homestay experiences where guests stay in a room within a family home, providing deeper cultural immersion. Luxury amenities are limited, and the focus is on authentic experiences rather than high-end facilities. What these accommodations lack in luxury, they make up for in personal service, cultural insights, and genuine hospitality. Visitors should adjust their expectations accordingly and embrace the opportunity to experience authentic island life rather than expecting resort-style amenities."},{"question":"Can I participate in fishing activities as a visitor to Kondey?","answer":"Yes, visitors to Kondey have excellent opportunities to participate in traditional fishing activities, which is one of the island''s main attractions. Most guesthouses can arrange for guests to join morning fishing trips on traditional dhonis, where you can learn pole-and-line fishing techniques from experienced local fishermen. Night fishing excursions are also popular, using hand lines to catch reef fish under the stars. Some accommodations offer more immersive experiences where visitors can participate in the entire process from catching fish to processing and cooking the catch. These activities provide not just entertainment but educational insights into sustainable fishing practices and maritime skills. The level of participation can be adjusted based on your interest and experience, from simple observation to active involvement. These experiences are weather-dependent and seasonal, so it''s advisable to be flexible with your schedule. Participating in these activities provides not only a unique experience but also supports the local fishing community and helps preserve traditional knowledge."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'kondey';


-- kudafaree
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Noonu Atoll, Northern Maldives"},{"label":"Island Type","value":"Inhabited Local Island"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 600 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"0.7 km long, 0.4 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Male","value":"180 km"},{"label":"Transfer Options","value":"Seaplane or domestic flight + speedboat"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Pristine beaches, excellent snorkeling, peaceful atmosphere"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Nature lovers, snorkelers, cultural travelers, budget travelers"}],"island_overview":["Nestled in the pristine waters of Noonu Atoll, Fodhdhoo Island represents the essence of authentic Maldivian island life. This charming local island offers visitors a unique opportunity to experience traditional culture while enjoying some of the most beautiful beaches in the northern Maldives.","Fodhdhoo stands out for its untouched natural beauty, crystal-clear lagoons, and vibrant house reef that''s perfect for snorkeling. The island maintains its traditional character while welcoming visitors with genuine Maldivian hospitality and warmth.","What makes Fodhdhoo truly special is its peaceful atmosphere, excellent marine life, and the opportunity to experience authentic island culture. Visitors can enjoy budget-friendly accommodations, delicious local cuisine, and unforgettable underwater adventures."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Fodhdhoo Island is strategically located in the central part of Noonu Atoll, approximately 180 kilometers from Male. This location ensures an authentic and peaceful experience while still offering excellent accessibility to the capital and international airport.","The island''s position provides natural protection from strong currents while maintaining access to some of the best snorkeling and diving sites in the Maldives. The surrounding waters feature healthy coral reefs and abundant marine life."]},{"heading":"Fodhdhoo: Natural Beauty & Marine Wonders","paragraphs":["Fodhdhoo Island is renowned for its exceptional natural beauty, featuring powder-white sand beaches, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and one of the most vibrant house reefs in Noonu Atoll. The island offers an unspoiled tropical paradise perfect for relaxation and marine exploration."]},{"heading":"Pristine White Sand Beaches","paragraphs":["Fodhdhoo boasts some of the most beautiful beaches in Noonu Atoll, with soft white sand and crystal-clear waters perfect for swimming and sunbathing."]},{"heading":"World-Class Snorkeling","paragraphs":["The island''s house reef is easily accessible from the beach and features diverse marine life, colorful corals, and excellent underwater visibility."]},{"heading":"Authentic Island Culture","paragraphs":["Experience genuine Maldivian hospitality and traditional island life in a peaceful setting away from commercial tourism."]},{"heading":"Pristine Sandbank Visits","paragraphs":["Explore nearby uninhabited sandbanks for the ultimate desert island experience with picnics and swimming in crystal-clear waters."]},{"heading":"Beach Highlights","paragraphs":["Fodhdhoo''s coastal features include:"]},{"heading":"Marine Environment","paragraphs":["The island''s underwater world features:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Fodhdhoo offers an excellent variety of activities focused on marine adventures, cultural experiences, and natural exploration. The island''s pristine environment provides perfect opportunities for both adventure and relaxation."]},{"heading":"House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["Explore the vibrant house reef directly from the beach, featuring colorful corals, tropical fish, and excellent underwater visibility."]},{"heading":"Scuba Diving Adventures","paragraphs":["Discover world-class dive sites around Noonu Atoll with professional dive operators offering courses and guided dives."]},{"heading":"Island Hopping Tours","paragraphs":["Visit nearby islands and discover uninhabited sandbanks, each offering unique experiences and pristine natural beauty."]},{"heading":"Traditional Night Fishing","paragraphs":["Join local fishermen for authentic night fishing experiences using traditional hand lines under the starlit Maldivian sky."]},{"heading":"Cultural Experiences","paragraphs":["Immerse yourself in local community life, learn traditional crafts, and experience authentic Maldivian customs and traditions."]},{"heading":"Sunset Cruises","paragraphs":["Enjoy magical sunset cruises around the atoll, often combined with dolphin watching and traditional dhoni sailing."]},{"heading":"People & Community Life","paragraphs":["Fodhdhoo is home to a close-knit community of approximately 600 residents who have preserved traditional Maldivian ways of life for generations. The island''s population is renowned for their warmth, hospitality, and strong community bonds."]},{"heading":"Daily Life","paragraphs":["Life on Fodhdhoo follows the natural rhythms of island living, beginning with morning prayers and continuing with fishing, community work, and family activities. The island maintains a peaceful, unhurried pace that reflects traditional Maldivian values."]},{"heading":"Culture & Traditions","paragraphs":["Fodhdhoo preserves authentic Maldivian cultural traditions including traditional music, dance, and handicrafts. The community celebrates Islamic festivals with enthusiasm and maintains traditional practices such as dhoni building and traditional fishing techniques."]},{"heading":"Local Economy","paragraphs":["The island''s economy is primarily based on fishing and increasingly tourism. Many families engage in traditional occupations while also participating in the growing tourism sector through guesthouses, restaurants, and tour services."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Fodhdhoo Island?","answer":"Regular ferry services are also available from Male and nearby islands in Noonu Atoll."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Fodhdhoo?","answer":"The best time to visit Fodhdhoo is during the dry season from December to April when weather conditions are most favorable. However, the island can be visited year-round, with the wet season (May-November) offering fewer crowds and lower accommodation rates."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Fodhdhoo?","answer":"Fodhdhoo offers various budget-friendly and mid-range accommodations including family guesthouses and beachfront properties. Most accommodations offer air conditioning, private bathrooms, and meal packages."},{"question":"What activities are available on Fodhdhoo?","answer":"Fodhdhoo offers excellent snorkeling from the house reef, diving excursions, island hopping tours, cultural experiences, traditional fishing trips, and sunset cruises. The island is particularly known for its pristine marine environment and authentic cultural experiences."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["foddhoo","manadhoo","velidhoo","miladhoo","maafaru","landhoo","kendhikolhudhoo","magoodhoo","henbandhoo","lhohi","maalhendhoo"]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'kudafaree';


-- kudahuvadhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Kudahuvadhoo Island?","answer":"Public ferry service operates regularly from Male (approximately 12 hours journey time). Private speedboat transfers can also be arranged through guesthouses (approximately 5 hours from Male)."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Kudahuvadhoo Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Kudahuvadhoo Island is during the northeast monsoon season (December to April), which brings dry, sunny weather with lower humidity and calmer seas. Water temperature remains warm (27-30C/80-86F) throughout the year, making it suitable for water activities year-round."},{"question":"What makes Kudahuvadhoo different from other local islands in the Maldives?","answer":"Kudahuvadhoo stands out as the administrative capital of Dhaalu Atoll with its domestic airport, historical significance, and blend of modern amenities with traditional culture. Unlike smaller islands, Kudahuvadhoo offers more services and infrastructure while serving as an excellent base for exploring Dhaalu Atoll''s dive sites."},{"question":"Are there any dress code requirements on Kudahuvadhoo Island?","answer":"As Kudahuvadhoo is a local inhabited island with a Muslim population, visitors are expected to dress modestly in public areas (shoulders and knees covered). Swimwear is only permitted at the designated \"bikini beach.\" When visiting the mosque or religious sites, women should cover their heads. These requirements don''t apply during water activities or at resort day visits."},{"question":"What marine life can I expect to see while diving in Dhaalu Atoll?","answer":"Dhaalu Atoll''s waters offer excellent marine biodiversity, including healthy coral formations with both hard and soft corals. Common sightings include reef sharks (particularly gray reef, whitetip and blacktip), various ray species, sea turtles, and abundant reef fish. The atoll''s channel dives often attract pelagic species like tuna and jackfish."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'kudahuvadhoo';


