-- kulhudhuffushi
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Kulhudhuffushi Island?","answer":"The most common route is a domestic flight to Hanimaadhoo Airport (1 hour from Male) followed by a 30-minute ferry to Kulhudhuffushi. Direct public ferry service operates weekly from Male (approximately 14 hours). Private speedboat transfers can be arranged but are more expensive."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Kulhudhuffushi?","answer":"The best time is during the northeast monsoon (December to April) with dry, sunny weather. The northern atolls can experience slightly different weather patterns than central/southern atolls. Cultural festivals often occur outside peak season."},{"question":"What makes Kulhudhuffushi different from other local islands?","answer":"As the capital of Haa Dhaalu Atoll, Kulhudhuffushi offers an urban Maldivian experience with more services, markets, and cultural facilities than smaller islands. It provides authentic local life with more amenities while maintaining strong northern traditions."},{"question":"Are there any dress code requirements on Kulhudhuffushi?","answer":"As a local island, modest dress is required in public areas (shoulders and knees covered). Swimwear is only permitted at the designated \"bikini beach.\" These requirements don''t apply during water activities or at resort day visits."},{"question":"What marine activities are available from Kulhudhuffushi?","answer":"While the immediate house reef is limited, boat trips to nearby reef systems offer excellent snorkeling and diving. Fishing excursions showcase northern techniques, and dolphin watching trips are popular. The island serves as a base for exploring Haa Dhaalu Atoll''s marine environment."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'kulhudhuffushi';


-- kumundhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Kumundhoo Island?","answer":"Due to the island''s remote location in the northern atolls, direct public ferry services from Male are limited. Most guesthouses can arrange the complete transfer from Male, including the domestic flight and speedboat connection. When planning your journey, remember that weather conditions can occasionally affect flight schedules in this region, so it''s advisable to allow buffer days in your travel plans. The journey to Kumundhoo is part of the adventure, offering beautiful aerial views of the Maldivian atolls during the flight and a chance to experience the stunning blue waters during the speedboat transfer."},{"question":"What makes Kumundhoo''s woodworking traditions unique in the Maldives?","answer":"Kumundhoo''s woodworking traditions stand out in the Maldives because the island has preserved comprehensive knowledge of traditional carpentry and woodcarving that combine various techniques while maintaining distinctly Maldivian characteristics. The island is particularly known for its lacquerware (known as \"liyelaa jehun\" in Dhivehi), where wooden items are coated with colored lacquer in intricate patterns, a specialized craft that requires exceptional skill and knowledge of natural materials. Kumundhoo craftsmen maintain expertise in traditional joinery techniques that create strong, durable furniture without relying on modern fasteners, demonstrating an intimate understanding of wood properties and structural principles. The island''s artisans have preserved knowledge of carving geometric and stylized natural patterns that reflect Islamic artistic traditions while incorporating elements unique to Maldivian culture. What makes Kumundhoo special is the integration of practical function with artistic expression, as even everyday items are created with attention to aesthetic detail and cultural significance. The community maintains specialized techniques for selecting, seasoning, and working with different wood types, including imported hardwoods and local varieties like coconut wood, each chosen for specific applications based on their properties. Kumundhoo is also known for its architectural woodwork, with skilled craftsmen creating decorative elements for mosques, homes, and community buildings that showcase the island''s woodworking heritage. These preserved traditions offer visitors insights into a sophisticated craft tradition that connects to centuries of Maldivian cultural heritage while demonstrating remarkable adaptation to the materials available in the island environment."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Kumundhoo Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Kumundhoo Island is during the northeast monsoon season (December to April), which brings dry, sunny weather with lower humidity and calmer seas. This period is ideal for water activities, with excellent visibility for snorkeling and diving. For those interested in experiencing the island''s woodworking traditions, this dry season is also excellent as many artisanal activities take place outdoors, and the drier air is better for woodworking and finishing processes. The southwest monsoon (May to November) brings occasional rain showers but also lower prices and fewer tourists. This season can still be good for cultural experiences and indoor woodworking demonstrations, though some outdoor activities may be affected by rain. Water temperature remains warm (27-30C/80-86F) throughout the year. Due to Kumundhoo''s northern location, it may experience slightly different weather patterns than southern atolls, with the possibility of brief rain showers even during the dry season. The shoulder months of November and April often offer a good balance of favorable weather and lower visitor numbers."},{"question":"What type of accommodation can I expect on Kumundhoo?","answer":"Accommodation on Kumundhoo is limited and simple, reflecting the island''s authentic character and minimal tourism development. The island offers a small number of family-run guesthouses that provide clean, comfortable rooms with basic amenities including air conditioning, private bathrooms with hot water, and Wi-Fi (though connectivity may be inconsistent). Most accommodations offer full-board packages that include three home-cooked Maldivian meals daily, featuring fresh seafood caught by local fishermen. Some woodworking families also offer homestay experiences where guests stay in a room within a family home, providing deeper cultural immersion and the opportunity to observe traditional carpentry up close. A few properties are located near the beach, offering easy access to the island''s beautiful shores. Luxury amenities are limited, and the focus is on authentic experiences rather than high-end facilities. What these accommodations lack in luxury, they make up for in personal service, cultural insights, and genuine hospitality. Visitors should adjust their expectations accordingly and embrace the opportunity to experience authentic island life rather than expecting resort-style amenities."},{"question":"Can I participate in woodworking activities as a visitor to Kumundhoo?","answer":"Yes, visitors to Kumundhoo have excellent opportunities to participate in woodworking activities, which is one of the island''s unique attractions. Most guesthouses can arrange for guests to join workshops where you can learn basic carpentry and carving techniques from skilled local artisans. These hands-on experiences allow you to create simple items like small carvings, decorative pieces, or practical objects while learning about the cultural significance of different designs and patterns. Wood selection demonstrations show how different types of wood are chosen for specific applications based on their properties and characteristics. Finishing technique sessions provide insights into traditional methods of treating and protecting wood, including natural oils, polishes, and lacquers. For those with a deeper interest, extended workshops can sometimes be arranged where you can learn more advanced techniques or work on larger projects over several days. Some accommodations offer more immersive experiences where visitors can stay with woodworking families, providing opportunities to observe and participate in the daily rhythm of this traditional craft. These activities provide not just entertainment but educational insights into an artisanal heritage that has shaped Maldivian material culture for centuries. The level of participation can be adjusted based on your interest and time available, from brief introductory sessions to more in-depth learning experiences."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'kumundhoo';


-- kunahandhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Laamu Atoll, Southern Maldives"},{"label":"Island Type","value":"Inhabited Local Island"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 700 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"0.9 km long, 0.5 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Male","value":"240 km"},{"label":"Transfer Options","value":"Domestic flight + speedboat/ferry"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Pristine house reef, crystal-clear waters, peaceful atmosphere"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Snorkelers, marine enthusiasts, cultural travelers, nature lovers"}],"island_overview":["Nestled in the crystal-clear waters of Laamu Atoll, Kunahandhoo Island offers visitors an extraordinary opportunity to experience pristine Maldivian island life. This enchanting local island combines breathtaking natural beauty with rich cultural traditions, creating an unforgettable tropical paradise experience.","Kunahandhoo stands out for its exceptional marine environment, featuring one of the most vibrant house reefs in the atoll and some of the clearest waters in the Maldives. The island has successfully maintained its authentic character while developing sustainable tourism that benefits the local community.","What makes Kunahandhoo truly remarkable is its perfect blend of adventure and tranquility. Visitors can enjoy world-class snorkeling, immerse themselves in authentic Maldivian culture, and relax on some of the most beautiful beaches in the southern Maldives, all while experiencing genuine local hospitality."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Kunahandhoo Island is perfectly positioned in the southern region of Laamu Atoll, approximately 240 kilometers from Male. This ideal location provides the perfect balance of accessibility and seclusion, offering visitors an authentic island experience in pristine surroundings.","The island''s strategic position within the atoll offers natural protection from strong currents while providing easy access to some of the best snorkeling and diving sites in the Maldives. The surrounding waters are renowned for their exceptional clarity and abundant marine biodiversity."]},{"heading":"Kunahandhoo: Pristine Paradise & Marine Wonderland","paragraphs":["Kunahandhoo Island is celebrated for its extraordinary natural beauty, featuring powder-white sand beaches, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and one of the most spectacular house reefs in Laamu Atoll. The island offers an untouched tropical paradise perfect for both relaxation and marine exploration."]},{"heading":"Spectacular White Sand Beaches","paragraphs":["Kunahandhoo boasts some of the most pristine beaches in Laamu Atoll, with soft white sand and crystal-clear waters perfect for swimming and sunbathing."]},{"heading":"World-Class House Reef","paragraphs":["The island''s house reef is easily accessible from shore and features exceptional marine biodiversity with colorful corals and abundant tropical fish."]},{"heading":"Authentic Island Culture","paragraphs":["Experience genuine Maldivian hospitality and traditional island life in a peaceful setting that has preserved its authentic character."]},{"heading":"Pristine Sandbank Excursions","paragraphs":["Explore nearby uninhabited sandbanks for the ultimate desert island experience with pristine beaches and crystal-clear lagoons."]},{"heading":"Beach Highlights","paragraphs":["Kunahandhoo''s coastal features include:"]},{"heading":"Marine Environment","paragraphs":["The island''s underwater ecosystem features:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Kunahandhoo offers an exceptional variety of activities that showcase the best of Maldivian marine life, culture, and natural beauty. The island''s pristine environment and rich cultural heritage provide endless opportunities for adventure and relaxation."]},{"heading":"House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["Explore the magnificent house reef directly from the beach, featuring vibrant corals, tropical fish, and exceptional underwater visibility."]},{"heading":"Scuba Diving Expeditions","paragraphs":["Discover world-class dive sites around Laamu Atoll with professional dive operators offering courses and guided underwater adventures."]},{"heading":"Island Hopping Tours","paragraphs":["Visit nearby islands and discover uninhabited sandbanks, each offering unique experiences and pristine natural beauty."]},{"heading":"Traditional Night Fishing","paragraphs":["Join local fishermen for authentic night fishing experiences using traditional hand lines under the magnificent starlit sky."]},{"heading":"Cultural Immersion","paragraphs":["Engage with the local community, learn traditional crafts, and experience authentic Maldivian customs and daily life."]},{"heading":"Sunset Cruises","paragraphs":["Enjoy magical sunset cruises around the atoll, often combined with dolphin watching and traditional dhoni sailing experiences."]},{"heading":"People & Community Life","paragraphs":["Kunahandhoo is home to a close-knit community of approximately 700 residents who have successfully preserved traditional Maldivian culture while embracing sustainable tourism. The island''s population is known for their exceptional warmth, hospitality, and strong community bonds."]},{"heading":"Island Lifestyle","paragraphs":["Daily life on Kunahandhoo follows the natural rhythms of island living, with the community engaging in fishing, small-scale agriculture, and tourism-related activities. The island maintains a peaceful, unhurried pace that reflects traditional Maldivian values and customs."]},{"heading":"Cultural Traditions","paragraphs":["Kunahandhoo preserves rich Maldivian cultural traditions including traditional music, dance, and handicrafts. The community celebrates Islamic festivals with great enthusiasm and maintains traditional practices such as dhoni boat building, traditional fishing techniques, and local cuisine preparation."]},{"heading":"Community Tourism","paragraphs":["The island has embraced community-based tourism that benefits local families while preserving the natural environment and cultural heritage. Many residents participate in tourism through guesthouses, restaurants, and tour services, creating sustainable economic opportunities."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Kunahandhoo Island?","answer":"Seaplane transfers are also available but depend on weather conditions. There''s also a weekly public ferry from Male that takes 14-16 hours."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Kunahandhoo?","answer":"The best time to visit Kunahandhoo is during the dry season from December to April when weather conditions are most favorable with minimal rainfall and calm seas. However, the island can be visited year-round, with the wet season (May-November) offering fewer crowds and lower accommodation rates."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Kunahandhoo?","answer":"Kunahandhoo offers various budget-friendly and mid-range accommodations including family guesthouses and beachfront properties. Most accommodations feature air conditioning, private bathrooms, and meal packages."},{"question":"What activities are available on Kunahandhoo?","answer":"Kunahandhoo offers excellent house reef snorkeling, diving excursions, island hopping tours, cultural experiences, traditional fishing trips, and sunset cruises. The island is particularly renowned for its spectacular house reef and crystal-clear waters with exceptional visibility."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["fonadhoo","hithadhoo","isdhoo","gan","maabaidhoo","mundoo","dhanbidhoo","maamendhoo","maavah"]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'kunahandhoo';


-- kunburudhoo-alif-dhaalu
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Kunburudhoo Island from Male?","answer":"You can reach Kunburudhoo Island from Male by public ferry, speedboat, or a combination of domestic flight and speedboat. For the quickest option, you can take a domestic flight to Maamigili Airport (about 30 minutes), followed by a 45-minute speedboat transfer to Kunburudhoo. Some guesthouses also offer private transfers for a higher fee."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Kunburudhoo Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Kunburudhoo Island is during the northeast monsoon (December-April), which generally provides the best overall weather conditions with less rainfall, lower humidity, and calmer seas. This period is ideal for snorkeling, diving, and beach activities. The water visibility is excellent during these months, making it perfect for marine life observation. The southwest monsoon (May-November) may have occasional rain showers but still offers many sunny days, fewer tourists, and lower prices. For whale shark sightings in nearby areas, the period from January to April is best. Water temperature remains warm (27-30C/80-86F) year-round, making Kunburudhoo a viable destination throughout the year."},{"question":"What makes Kunburudhoo different from other local islands in the Maldives?","answer":"Kunburudhoo stands out from other local islands in the Maldives primarily because of its peaceful, authentic atmosphere. Unlike more developed tourist destinations, Kunburudhoo maintains its traditional way of life with fewer visitors and a more relaxed pace. The island offers excellent snorkeling right from shore, beautiful beaches without crowds, and genuine interactions with the local community. While it has fewer facilities than larger islands, Kunburudhoo provides a more immersive cultural experience at a lower cost than resorts. The small size of the island creates an intimate atmosphere where visitors quickly feel at home, making it ideal for travelers seeking tranquility and authenticity."},{"question":"Are there any dress code requirements on Kunburudhoo Island?","answer":"Yes, as Kunburudhoo is a local inhabited island with a Muslim population, visitors are expected to dress modestly in public areas. Both men and women should cover shoulders and knees when walking around the village, visiting shops, or dining in local restaurants. Swimwear (including bikinis) is only permitted at the designated \"bikini beach\" area on the eastern side of the island. When visiting the mosque or religious sites, women should cover their heads with a scarf. These dress code requirements are a sign of respect for local culture and traditions and are generally well-enforced on the island."},{"question":"What marine life can I expect to see while snorkeling around Kunburudhoo?","answer":"Kunburudhoo''s house reef offers excellent snorkeling with diverse marine life. You can expect to see colorful reef fish including parrotfish, angelfish, butterflyfish, and triggerfish. Blacktip reef sharks are commonly seen, especially in the early morning and late afternoon. Various ray species including eagle rays and stingrays frequent the area, and lucky snorkelers might spot hawksbill or green sea turtles. The healthy coral formations provide habitat for moray eels, octopuses, and countless other reef creatures. For more spectacular marine encounters like manta rays and whale sharks, you can join boat trips to nearby sites in Alifu Dhaalu Atoll, known for these magnificent creatures (seasonal)."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'kunburudhoo-alif-dhaalu';


-- kurendhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Lhaviyani Atoll, Northern Maldives"},{"label":"Island Type","value":"Inhabited Local Island"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 1,200 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"0.8 km long, 0.4 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Male","value":"185 km"},{"label":"Transfer Options","value":"Seaplane or domestic flight + speedboat"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Beautiful beaches, excellent snorkeling, peaceful atmosphere"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Beach lovers, snorkelers, cultural travelers, budget travelers"}],"island_overview":["Kurendhoo Island is a peaceful local island in Lhaviyani Atoll that offers visitors an authentic taste of traditional Maldivian life. This charming island combines natural beauty with cultural richness, providing an ideal destination for travelers seeking genuine island experiences.","Known for its pristine beaches, crystal-clear waters, and vibrant house reef, Kurendhoo provides excellent opportunities for snorkeling, diving, and marine exploration. The island''s friendly community welcomes visitors with traditional Maldivian hospitality and warmth.","What makes Kurendhoo special is its perfect balance of natural beauty and cultural authenticity. Visitors can enjoy beautiful beaches, explore marine life, and experience traditional island life while staying in comfortable, budget-friendly accommodations."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Kurendhoo Island is located in the northern part of Lhaviyani Atoll, approximately 185 kilometers from Male. The island''s position provides easy access to some of the best snorkeling and diving sites in the atoll while maintaining a peaceful, secluded atmosphere.","The island''s location offers protection from strong currents while providing access to vibrant coral reefs and diverse marine life. Its proximity to other islands in the atoll makes it an excellent base for island hopping adventures."]},{"heading":"Kurendhoo: Natural Paradise & Marine Wonders","paragraphs":["Kurendhoo Island is blessed with exceptional natural beauty, featuring pristine white sand beaches, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and one of the most accessible house reefs in Lhaviyani Atoll. The island offers perfect conditions for beach relaxation and marine exploration."]},{"heading":"Pristine White Sand Beaches","paragraphs":["Kurendhoo features beautiful white sand beaches with gentle slopes and calm waters, perfect for swimming, sunbathing, and beach activities."]},{"heading":"Excellent House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["The island''s house reef is easily accessible from the beach and offers excellent snorkeling with diverse marine life and colorful corals."]},{"heading":"Peaceful Island Atmosphere","paragraphs":["Experience the tranquil pace of traditional island life with friendly locals and authentic Maldivian culture and hospitality."]},{"heading":"Nearby Sandbank Adventures","paragraphs":["Explore pristine sandbanks and uninhabited islands around Kurendhoo for the ultimate tropical paradise experience."]},{"heading":"Beach Features","paragraphs":["Kurendhoo''s coastal highlights include:"]},{"heading":"Marine Life","paragraphs":["The waters around Kurendhoo feature:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Kurendhoo offers a perfect blend of marine adventures, cultural experiences, and relaxation opportunities. The island''s pristine environment and friendly community provide ideal conditions for various activities."]},{"heading":"House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["Explore the vibrant house reef directly from the beach, featuring colorful corals, tropical fish, and excellent underwater visibility."]},{"heading":"Scuba Diving Excursions","paragraphs":["Discover nearby dive sites with professional dive operators offering guided dives and certification courses."]},{"heading":"Island Hopping Adventures","paragraphs":["Visit nearby islands, pristine sandbanks, and discover the diverse beauty of Lhaviyani Atoll."]},{"heading":"Traditional Fishing","paragraphs":["Experience authentic Maldivian fishing techniques with local fishermen during sunset and night fishing trips."]},{"heading":"Cultural Immersion","paragraphs":["Learn about local traditions, visit community areas, and experience authentic Maldivian island life."]},{"heading":"Sunset Cruises","paragraphs":["Enjoy magical sunset cruises around the atoll, often combined with dolphin watching and traditional dhoni sailing."]},{"heading":"Community Life & Culture","paragraphs":["Kurendhoo is home to approximately 1,200 residents who maintain traditional Maldivian ways of life while embracing sustainable tourism. The island''s community is known for their friendliness, hospitality, and strong cultural traditions."]},{"heading":"Island Life","paragraphs":["Daily life on Kurendhoo follows traditional patterns centered around fishing, family, and community activities. The island maintains a peaceful atmosphere where visitors can experience authentic Maldivian culture and customs."]},{"heading":"Local Traditions","paragraphs":["The community preserves traditional Maldivian practices including traditional music, dance, handicrafts, and fishing techniques. Visitors can observe and sometimes participate in cultural activities and celebrations."]},{"heading":"Sustainable Tourism","paragraphs":["Kurendhoo has embraced sustainable tourism practices that benefit the local community while preserving the island''s natural environment and cultural heritage for future generations."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Kurendhoo Island?","answer":"Regular ferry services are also available from Male and nearby islands in Lhaviyani Atoll."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Kurendhoo?","answer":"The best time to visit Kurendhoo is during the dry season from December to April when weather conditions are most favorable for beach activities and water sports. However, the island can be visited year-round with the wet season offering fewer crowds and lower prices."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Kurendhoo?","answer":"Kurendhoo offers various budget-friendly accommodations including family guesthouses and beachfront properties. Most accommodations offer air conditioning, private bathrooms, and meal packages."},{"question":"What activities are available on Kurendhoo?","answer":"Kurendhoo offers excellent snorkeling from the house reef, diving excursions, island hopping tours, traditional fishing trips, cultural experiences, and sunset cruises. The island is particularly known for its accessible house reef and peaceful atmosphere."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["hinnavaru","naifaru","olhuvelifushi"]}'::jsonb
